## Component Documentation

### DeveloperTools
The main container component for SDK and API documentation.

### ToolSection
Represents a major section of developer tools (SDK or API).

Props:
- `title`: string - The section title
- `type`: 'library' | 'interface' - The type of developer tool
- `description`: string - A brief description of the tool's purpose

### ToolFeature
Represents a specific feature or capability within a tool section.

Props:
- `feature`: string - The specific feature or capability
- `type`: 'validation' | 'testing' | 'submission' | 'endpoint' | 'authentication' - The type of feature
- `importance`: 'high' | 'medium' | 'low' - The importance level of the feature
- `description`: string - A brief description of the feature's purpose

## Usage Example

```tsx
<DeveloperTools>
  <ToolSection
    title="Example Tool"
    type="library"
    description="Example developer tool"
  >
    <ToolFeature
      feature="Example feature"
      type="validation"
      importance="high"
      description="Example feature description"
    />
  </ToolSection>
</DeveloperTools>
```

## Notes
- Each tool section should have a clear, specific focus
- Features should be ordered by importance
- All endpoints and capabilities should be clearly documented
- Maintain consistency in feature types and importance levels
- Update features as the SDK and API evolve
- Include authentication and security considerations
- Document rate limits and usage guidelines
